    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d2">

                <pb facs="0111" n="1" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg1"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.51 War Credits/482½: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Skinner</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-12-08T12:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 8,
                                1927—noon</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>42. Reference your 66, December 7, 5 p.m. The attitude of the Department toward
                    financing for the benefit of Greece, done in the United States, as set forth
                    previously (see its telegram 37, November 18, 6 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d2-f1"
                    />), cannot be modified until the financial settlement (which was outlined in
                    the Department’s circular telegram dated December 5, 7 p.m.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d2-f2"/>) has been approved by the Greek Parliament. Guarded use of
                    this information is permitted you.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
